{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## IMPLEMENTED-3B5F: Gerrit 1393 pushed (522+/1153-). NOT verified by me, NOT closed.\n\nSubagent implemented the attested plan. Change **1393** (`72e7988419`, branch `3b5f-tombstone`, worktree\n`/Users/joeoakhart/3b5f-impl`), awaiting `Verified +1` / `LLM-Review +1`. Net ~630 lines DELETED, which is\nthe shape a dead-chain removal should have.\n\n### Reported evidence (subagent's, not independently re-run by me)\n\n* **RED-first**: 6 failed / 3 passed before implementation, 9/9 after. The load-bearing red reproduced the\n  resurrection against a **real** `BindingStore` driven to retirement the production way — 3x\n  confirmed-404 `note_absent` — rather than by hand-writing `bindings-retired.json`.\n* **Mutation check**: reverting ONLY the 4-line guard in `_compute_outbound_create_mutation` re-failed\n  exactly the three behavioural cells (no-create, never-bound-still-creates, observability) while the\n  fail-open and WIRE-trap cells stayed green — correct, they do not depend on the guard.\n* Gates: `make lint`, `make typecheck` (432 files), `pytest tests/unit` **8035 passed / 28 skipped / 0\n  failed**. `outbound_differ.py` is 798/800 — verified independently.\n* All three traps respected: the suppression stays and is pinned by a test; the port capability\n  (`probe_remote` / `SupportsAbsenceProbe` / `inbound_probe.py` / both adapter impls) is untouched with\n  follow-up [rebar:f020-0960-2c42-4d61] filed; symbol removals were grep-checked as strings.\n\n### The judgement calls a reviewer should look at FIRST\n\nThe subagent flagged these itself, which is the right instinct — none is obviously wrong, none is\nobviously fine:\n\n1. **Scope creep that is arguably correct**: it also removed `reconcile_helpers._audit_log_probe`,\n   `_build_hard_delete_recreate` and the `pending_hard_delete_creates` plumbing, on the reasoning that\n   removing only the call sites would orphan the builders — the exact objection `review-plan` raised\n   against leaving `_apply_inbound_delete` behind. Consistent with the plan's intent; wider than its\n   literal text.\n2. **`mutation._VALID_COMBINATIONS` still permits `(inbound, delete)` / `(inbound, probe)`.** Only the\n   leaves and dispatch entries are gone, so such a mutation would now raise `UnknownActionError` rather\n   than being rejected up front. Deliberately left because the plan did not ask to narrow the allowlist\n   and the existing tests assert `_LEAVES ⊆ _VALID_COMBINATIONS`, not the reverse. Defensible, but it is\n   a loose end someone should agree to.\n3. **`docs/env-vars.md` changed** — one file beyond the declared `file_impact`. It is generated and gated\n   by `test_gen_env_registry.py`; removing `_apply_inbound_delete` shifted an `os.environ.get(<non-literal>)`\n   line number. The subagent confirmed that test passes on the pre-change tree, so it is a consequence of\n   this change rather than pre-existing.\n4. `is_retired_local` is built on a new `retired_key_for_local(local_id) -> str | None` primitive so the\n   suppression message can NAME the retired key and `unretire(<key>)`. Both public; the plan's signature\n   is honoured.\n\n**Do not close 3b5f on this report.** Verify against the acceptance criteria and wait for both Gerrit\ngates — a passing local suite is not `Verified +1`."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785878598883963001,"uuid":"d75d4a3a-b69a-48df-88ab-578491dd7618"}